  <!-- Headline -->
  <h2>What Actually Makes Saily Different</h2>
  <p>
    Saily is NordVPN's eSIM spin-off, built by the same company (Nord Security) rather than merely "partnered with" them, and that shows up in the product itself: every Saily plan ships with ad blocking, malware/phishing site blocking, and a virtual-location tool baked in, rather than connectivity being the whole product. If you don't care about any of that and just want the cheapest GB, it's not a reason to pick Saily over <a href="/airalo/">Airalo</a>. But if you're the type who'd normally pay for a VPN separately when traveling, it's already in the box.
  </p>
  <p>
    Saily also sells one universal eSIM instead of a separate profile per region the way most competitors do. Once it's installed, it keeps working as you cross into a new supported country. You're not reinstalling or swapping eSIMs at each border.
  </p>

